'''Li'l Doge''' (ちびわんこ, ''Chibi Wanko'', '''Li'l Doggy''') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. They were added in [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Li'l Doge
|image = E 608.png
|first appearance = '''UL''': [[Tear-Soaked Puppy|Sub-chapter 44 - Tear-Soaked Puppy]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Automatic Avoidance|Sub-chapter 16 - Automatic Avoidance]]
|money drop = 30¢ - 118¢
}}

==Enemy==
[[Doge]]'s time-travelling grandchild possesses negligible health and damage like their grandfather. However, they have a relatively high movement speed, akin to [[Doge Dark]]. Combined with a 20% chance of dodging your cats' attacks, Li'l Doge could lock the battleground and prevent said units from progressing, especially when spawned en masse.

==Strategy==
Just like many other Doge variants and your dodge-reliant meatshields, Li'l Doge abuses weak hits from your units (i.e., meatshields) to their advantage. While many units can OHKO Li'l Doge, things will quickly turn awry if Li'l Doge does dodge as they will effectively stall them (unless the units in question have abilities allowing them to hit beyond their range) in a fashion similar to [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]].

Due the rarity of the Curse ability, especially against Traitless, you may have to rely on the [[Ototo Corps|Curseblast Cannon]] for a window of opportunity before you could wipe the field clean of Li'l Doges.

