==Trivia==
*Li'l Doge's description may be a reference to the overall plot of ''Doraemon'', in which the poverty-stricken [[wikia:Doraemon:Sewashi Nobi|Sewashi]] alters the past by assisting his failure of a great-great-grandfather [[wikia:Doraemon:Nobita Nobi|Nobita]]; the main difference is that Li'l Doge is implied to help [[Doge]] directly, rather letting [[wikia:Doraemon:Doraemon (character)|Doraemon]] handle the bulk of the work. Hence, unlike Sewashi, who is mostly successful, Li'l Doge's inability to comprehend past exams greatly impeded its attempts to alter future. Doge and Nobita are both known for their poor academics, which further strengthens this reference.
*Li'l Doge is the first non-collab enemy and the second enemy overall to have the Dodge Attack ability, the first being [[MikuDoge]].
**Both enemies share the exact same Dodge chance and duration, along with both happening to be variants of Doge.
*Ironically, Li'l Doge has higher health and attack power than Doge.

